//! Parity of the multi-objective acquisition functions with BoTorch
//! (fixtures in `tests/fixtures/phase5b/*.json`, generated by
//! `scripts/generate_fixtures.py --phase 5b` with BoTorch main and
//! `--phase 5b-3392` with a BoTorch that includes meta-pytorch/botorch#3392):
//!
//! * the multi-output objectives (identity with `outcomes`, weighted,
//!   generic, feasibility-weighted) on samples;
//! * values and gradients of qEHVI and qLogEHVI (q = 1, 2, 3, t-batches,
//!   pending points, outcome constraints with `eta`, `fat`, `tau_relu`,
//!   objectives, exact and approximate partitionings, whose cells must
//!   match BoTorch's), qNEHVI and qLogNEHVI (`cache_root` true / false,
//!   incremental or not, `alpha`, constraints, objectives, pending points
//!   at construction, cached or not, pruned baselines) with their state
//!   (cached baseline, number of cells, per-sample hypervolumes, the
//!   improvement of cached pending points), the analytic EHVI and
//!   qLogNParEGO; `prune_inferior_points_multi_objective`,
//!   `get_default_partitioning_alpha` and `compute_subset_indices`;
//!   on multi-output models with m = 2, 3, 4 and a `ModelListGP`;
//! * against a BoTorch with meta-pytorch/botorch#3392: NEHVI after sequences
//!   of `set_X_pending` calls that cache pending points, and the
//!   feasibility weighting with two constraint indices.
//!
//! All MC quantities use BoTorch's recorded base samples, installed in
//! samplers whose own seed differs from BoTorch's (a dimension without a
//! recorded draw would change the values). Tolerances: values 1e-9
//! (relative; log values absolute below 1), gradients 1e-8 (relative to the
//! largest component, entries within 1e-14 count as equal) or 10 times
//! BoTorch's own change under 1e-14 perturbations of the training inputs
//! (the noise floor of NEHVI and qLogNParEGO over the training points),
//! whichever is larger. Discrete outputs (cells, pruned sets, cached
//! baselines, subsets) must be identical. Run with `--nocapture` to print the
//! error tables.

mod common;

